## Common Patterns

### Storage Operations
```typescript
try {
  const session = storage.get<CoachingSession>(`session:${id}`, defaultSession);
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Storage error:', error);
}
storage.set<CoachingSession>(`session:${id}`, updated);
```

### Error Handling
```typescript
export const getCurriculum = (id: string) => {
  const c = REGISTRY[id];
  if (!c) throw new Error('Curriculum not found: ' + id);
  return c;
};
```

### React Hooks Pattern
```typescript
export function useStudents() {
  const [students, setStudents] = useState<Student[]>([]);
  useEffect(() => {
    setStudents(storage.get<Student[]>('students', []));
  }, []);
  const addStudent = (student: Student) => {
    const updated = [...students, student];
    setStudents(updated);
    storage.set('students', updated);
  };
  return { students, addStudent };
}
```

### PrimeReact Usage
```typescript
import { Button } from 'primereact/button';
import { Dropdown } from 'primereact/dropdown';
```

---

## Important Business Rules

### Session Management
- Sessions are immutable; observations are append-only
- Observations maintain chronological order
- All timestamps in ISO format
- Session IDs are UUIDs

### Curriculum Access
- Curriculum data is read-only
- Use `getCurriculum(id)` from `curriculumService.ts`
- IDs follow hierarchical patterns

### Assessment Recording
- Confidence scale: 1, 2, 3
- Next actions: 'Teach' | 'Review' | 'Reteach'
- Persist immediately to localStorage

### Data Persistence
- Use `core/services/storageService.ts`
- Handle failures gracefully
- Fallback to empty arrays/objects on error

